- op: discuss  # cba4
  at: '2026-06-07T06:41:21Z'  # cba4
  by: agent  # cba4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cba4
  clock: 2  # cba4
  nonce: cba4  # cba4
  message: "Dogfood finding (member F147.A1-b, split from F147.A1), reproduces on the frozen substrate. Mechanism: the documented contract routes WebSocket sends to an event_publishes edge carrying meta[\"channel_kind\"]=\"websocket\". Instead, WS detection emits references/calls edges (file-anchor -> synthetic endpoint node) carrying a raw meta.channel key, with no channel_kind, no protocol, and no framework. The evidence lives under a different edge type and a different, undocumented meta key. Scope: 42 WS-channel edges (30 references + 12 calls) carry raw meta.channel and zero carry channel_kind; affects WS detection on any repo. Exposure/consequence: a consumer following the documented contract to find WebSocket channels by filtering event_publishes where channel_kind==\"websocket\" gets zero results; an agent enumerating message channels by the contract entirely misses WebSocket communication, then reasons about a graph that omits it. Expectation (spec table): WS sends surface as event_publishes edges discriminated by meta.channel_kind=\"websocket\". Related but distinct from WI-zamum (meta.channel undocumented in spec/schema), WI-pozom (meta.channel referent overload across edge types), WI-vovob (meta.channel duplicates meta.topic) — those concern the meta.channel key itself; THIS row is the wrong-edge-type routing + missing channel_kind discriminator on WS sends, which has its own fix (route WS to event_publishes with channel_kind=websocket). Also distinct from WI-bumug's sibling WI-... channel_kind value-space collapse folded onto INV-lifik. Cross-ref WI-zamum, WI-pozom, WI-vovob, INV-lifik."  # cba4
